{"name":"Bogart","hex":"#8b8274","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bogart","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An English surname from Dutch, most famously borne by American actor Humphrey Bogart."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To behave in a manner similar to the on-screen characters portrayed by Humphrey Bogart."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bogart"}],"entries":[{"title":"Humphrey Bogart","blocks":[{"text":"Humphrey DeForest Bogart, nicknamed Bogie, was an American actor. Often known for his leading roles as both gangsters and detectives in film noirs, his performances in classic Hollywood cinema made him an American cultural icon. He won an Academy Award and was honored with a star on the Hollywood Walk of Fame in 1960."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Humphrey_Bogart_by_Elmer_Fryer_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Humphrey_Bogart_by_Elmer_Fryer_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Humphrey_Bogart","wikidata":"Q16390"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/245_W103_St_Bogie_plaque_jeh.JPG/500px-245_W103_St_Bogie_plaque_jeh.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/245_W103_St_Bogie_plaque_jeh.JPG/1280px-245_W103_St_Bogie_plaque_jeh.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/245_W103_St_Bogie_plaque_jeh.JPG/500px-245_W103_St_Bogie_plaque_jeh.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Plaque commemorating Bogart's birthplace, 245 W. 103rd St., New York City","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A245_W103_St_Bogie_plaque_jeh.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Maud_Humphrey_from_Am